\s1 Xerxes’ Royal Feast
\p \v 1 \w This is what happened|strong="H1961"\w* \w in the days|strong="H3117"\w* \w of Xerxes|strong="H325"\w*,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa Ahasuerus\ft ; here and throughout Esther \f* \w who reigned over|strong="H4427"\w* \w 127|strong="H7651"\w* \w provinces|strong="H4082"\w* \w from India|strong="H1912"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w Cush|strong="H3568"\w*.\f + \fr 1:1 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* \v 2 \w In those|strong="H1992"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w* \w sat|strong="H3427"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w his royal|strong="H4438"\w* \w throne|strong="H3678"\w* \w in the citadel|strong="H1002"\w* \w of Susa|strong="H7800"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w In the third|strong="H7969"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of his reign|strong="H4427"\w*, \w Xerxes held|strong="H6213"\w* \w a feast|strong="H4960"\w* \w for all|strong="H3605"\w* \w his officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w and servants|strong="H5650"\w*. \w The military leaders|strong="H2428"\w* \w of Persia|strong="H6539"\w* \w and Media|strong="H4074"\w* \w were there|strong="H6440"\w*, \w along with the nobles|strong="H6579"\w* \w and princes|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the provinces|strong="H4082"\w*. \v 4 \w And for a full|strong="H7227"\w* \w 180|strong="H8084"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w he displayed|strong="H7200"\w* \w the glorious|strong="H3519"\w* \w riches|strong="H6239"\w* \w of his kingdom|strong="H4438"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w the magnificent|strong="H8597"\w* \w splendor|strong="H3366"\w* \w of his greatness|strong="H1420"\w*.
\p \v 5 \w At the end|strong="H4390"\w* \w of this|strong="H428"\w* \w time|strong="H3117"\w*, \w in the garden|strong="H1594"\w* \w court|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the royal|strong="H4428"\w* \w palace|strong="H1055"\w*, \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w held|strong="H6213"\w* \w a seven-day|strong="H7651"\w* \w feast|strong="H4960"\w* \w for all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w in the citadel|strong="H1002"\w* \w of Susa|strong="H7800"\w*, \w from the least|strong="H6996"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w the greatest|strong="H1419"\w*. \v 6 \w Hangings of white|strong="H2353"\w* \w and blue|strong="H8504"\w* \w linen|strong="H3768"\w* \w were fastened|strong="H270"\w* \w with cords|strong="H2256"\w* \w of fine white|strong="H948"\w* \w and purple material|strong="H713"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w rings|strong="H1550"\w* \w on the marble|strong="H8336"\w* \w pillars|strong="H5982"\w*. \w Gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w and silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w couches|strong="H4296"\w* \w were arranged|strong="H5921"\w* \w on a mosaic pavement|strong="H7531"\w* \w of porphyry|strong="H923"\w*, \w marble|strong="H8336"\w*, \w mother-of-pearl|strong="H1858"\w*, \w and other costly stones|strong="H5508"\w*.
\p \v 7 \w Beverages were served|strong="H8248"\w* \w in an array of goblets|strong="H3627"\w* \w of gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w each|strong="H3627"\w* \w with a different design|strong="H8138"\w*, \w and the royal|strong="H4438"\w* \w wine|strong="H3196"\w* \w flowed freely|strong="H7227"\w*, \w according to the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w bounty|strong="H3027"\w*. \v 8 \w By|strong="H1881"\w* \w order|strong="H3245"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w no|strong="H369"\w* \w limit was placed|strong="H597"\w* \w on the drinking|strong="H8360"\w*, \w and every|strong="H3605"\w* \w official|strong="H7227"\w* \w of his household|strong="H1004"\w* \w was to serve|strong="H6213"\w* \w each|strong="H376"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w* \w whatever he desired|strong="H7522"\w*.
\s1 Queen Vashti’s Refusal
\p \v 9 \w Queen|strong="H4436"\w* \w Vashti|strong="H2060"\w* \w also|strong="H1571"\w* \w gave|strong="H6213"\w* \w a banquet|strong="H4960"\w* \w for the women|strong="H802"\w* \w in the royal|strong="H4438"\w* \w palace|strong="H1004"\w* \w of King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w On the seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*, \w when the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w heart|strong="H3820"\w* \w was merry|strong="H2895"\w* \w with wine|strong="H3196"\w*, \w he ordered|strong="H559"\w* \w the seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w eunuchs|strong="H5631"\w* \w who served|strong="H8334"\w* \w him|strong="H325"\w* — \w Mehuman|strong="H4104"\w*, \w Biztha|strong="H968"\w*, \w Harbona|strong="H2726"\w*, \w Bigtha|strong="H903"\w*, \w Abagtha|strong="H5"\w*, \w Zethar|strong="H2242"\w*, \w and Carkas|strong="H3752"\w* — \v 11 \w to bring|strong="H935"\w* \w Queen|strong="H4436"\w* \w Vashti|strong="H2060"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w him|strong="H4428"\w*, \w wearing her royal|strong="H4438"\w* \w crown|strong="H3804"\w*, \w to display|strong="H7200"\w* \w her beauty|strong="H3308"\w* \w to the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w and officials|strong="H8269"\w*. \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w she was|strong="H1931"\w* \w beautiful|strong="H2896"\w* \w to behold|strong="H4758"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w Queen|strong="H4436"\w* \w Vashti, however|strong="H2060"\w*, \w refused|strong="H3985"\w* \w to come|strong="H935"\w* \w at the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w command|strong="H1697"\w* \w brought by|strong="H3027"\w* \w his eunuchs|strong="H5631"\w*. \w And the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w became furious|strong="H7107"\w*, \w and his anger|strong="H2534"\w* \w burned|strong="H1197"\w* within him.
\s1 Queen Vashti Deposed
\p \v 13 \w Then the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w consulted|strong="H559"\w* \w the wise men|strong="H2450"\w* \w who knew|strong="H3045"\w* \w the times|strong="H6256"\w*, \w for it was|strong="H3588"\w* \w customary|strong="H3651"\w* \w for him|strong="H4428"\w* \w to confer|strong="H1697"\w* \w with|strong="H6440"\w* \w the experts|strong="H3045"\w* \w in law|strong="H1881"\w* \w and justice|strong="H1779"\w*. \v 14 \w His closest advisors were|strong="H7138"\w* \w Carshena|strong="H3771"\w*, \w Shethar|strong="H8369"\w*, \w Admatha|strong="H133"\w*, \w Tarshish|strong="H8659"\w*, \w Meres|strong="H4825"\w*, \w Marsena|strong="H4826"\w*, \w and Memucan|strong="H4462"\w*, \w the seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w princes|strong="H8269"\w* \w of Persia|strong="H6539"\w* \w and Media|strong="H4074"\w* \w who had personal access to|strong="H7200"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and ranked|strong="H3427"\w* \w highest|strong="H7223"\w* \w in the kingdom|strong="H4438"\w*.
\p \v 15 “\w According to law|strong="H1881"\w*,” \w he asked, “what|strong="H4100"\w* \w should be done|strong="H6213"\w* \w with Queen|strong="H4436"\w* \w Vashti|strong="H2060"\w*, \w since|strong="H5921"\w* \w she refused to obey|strong="H3808"\w* \w the command|strong="H3982"\w* \w of King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w* \w delivered by|strong="H3027"\w* \w the eunuchs|strong="H5631"\w*?”
\p \v 16 \w And in the presence|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and his princes|strong="H8269"\w*, \w Memucan|strong="H4462"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Queen|strong="H4436"\w* \w Vashti|strong="H2060"\w* \w has wronged|strong="H5753"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* \w only|strong="H905"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w but|strong="H3588"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the princes|strong="H8269"\w* \w and the peoples|strong="H5971"\w* \w in all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the provinces|strong="H4082"\w* \w of King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w*. \v 17 \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w the conduct|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the queen|strong="H4436"\w* \w will become known|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w women|strong="H802"\w*, \w causing them to despise|strong="H959"\w* \w their husbands|strong="H1167"\w*\f + \fr 1:17 \ft Or \fqa to disdain their husbands in their eyes\f* \w and say|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w* \w ordered|strong="H559"\w* \w Queen|strong="H4436"\w* \w Vashti|strong="H2060"\w* \w to be brought|strong="H935"\w* \w before him|strong="H6440"\w*, \w but she did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w come|strong="H935"\w*.’
\p \v 18 \w This|strong="H2088"\w* \w very day|strong="H3117"\w* \w the noble women|strong="H8282"\w* \w of Persia|strong="H6539"\w* \w and Media|strong="H4074"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w have heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w about|strong="H853"\w* \w the queen’s|strong="H4436"\w* \w conduct|strong="H1697"\w* \w will say|strong="H559"\w* \w the same thing to all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w officials|strong="H8269"\w*, \w resulting in much|strong="H1767"\w* \w contempt|strong="H963"\w* \w and wrath|strong="H7110"\w*.
\p \v 19 \w So if|strong="H518"\w* \w it pleases|strong="H2896"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w let him issue|strong="H3318"\w* \w a royal|strong="H4438"\w* \w decree|strong="H1697"\w*, \w and let it be recorded|strong="H3789"\w* \w in the laws|strong="H1881"\w* \w of Persia|strong="H6539"\w* \w and Media|strong="H4074"\w* \w so that it cannot|strong="H3808"\w* \w be repealed|strong="H5674"\w*, \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Vashti|strong="H2060"\w* \w shall never again|strong="H3808"\w* \w enter|strong="H935"\w* \w the presence|strong="H6440"\w* \w of King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w*, \w and that her royal position|strong="H4438"\w* \w shall be given|strong="H5414"\w* \w to a woman|strong="H7468"\w* \w better|strong="H2896"\w* \w than she|strong="H4480"\w*. \v 20 \w The edict|strong="H6599"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w issues|strong="H6213"\w* \w will be heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w throughout|strong="H3605"\w* \w his vast|strong="H7227"\w* \w kingdom|strong="H4438"\w* — \w and so|strong="H3588"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w women|strong="H802"\w*, \w from the least|strong="H6996"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w the greatest|strong="H1419"\w*, \w will honor|strong="H5414"\w* \w their husbands|strong="H1167"\w*.”
\p \v 21 \w The king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and his princes|strong="H8269"\w* \w were pleased|strong="H3190"\w* \w with this counsel|strong="H1697"\w*; \w so the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w did|strong="H6213"\w* \w as Memucan|strong="H4462"\w* \w advised|strong="H1697"\w*. \v 22 \w He sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w letters|strong="H5612"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the provinces|strong="H4082"\w* \w of the kingdom|strong="H4428"\w*, \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w each province|strong="H4082"\w* \w in its own script|strong="H3791"\w* \w and to|strong="H413"\w* \w each people|strong="H5971"\w* \w in their own language|strong="H3956"\w*, \w proclaiming|strong="H1696"\w*\f + \fr 1:22 \ft Literally \fqa proclaiming in the language of his own people\f* \w that every|strong="H3605"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w* \w should be|strong="H1961"\w* \w master|strong="H8323"\w* \w of his own household|strong="H1004"\w*.
\c 2
\s1 Seeking Vashti’s Successor
\p \v 1 \w Some time later|strong="H310"\w*, \w when the anger|strong="H2534"\w* \w of King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w* \w had subsided|strong="H7918"\w*, \w he remembered|strong="H2142"\w* \w Vashti|strong="H2060"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w she had done|strong="H6213"\w*, \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w had been decreed|strong="H1504"\w* \w against her|strong="H5921"\w*.
\p \v 2 \w Then the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w attendants|strong="H5288"\w* \w proposed|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Let a search be made|strong="H1245"\w* \w for beautiful|strong="H2896"\w* \w young|strong="H5291"\w* \w virgins|strong="H1330"\w* \w for the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \v 3 \w and let the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w appoint|strong="H6485"\w* \w commissioners|strong="H6496"\w* \w in each|strong="H3605"\w* \w province|strong="H4082"\w* \w of his kingdom|strong="H4438"\w* \w to assemble|strong="H6908"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the beautiful|strong="H2896"\w* \w young|strong="H5291"\w* \w women|strong="H1330"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the harem|strong="H1004"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the citadel|strong="H1002"\w* \w of Susa|strong="H7800"\w*. \w Let them be placed|strong="H413"\w* \w under the care|strong="H3027"\w* \w of Hegai|strong="H1896"\w*, \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w eunuch|strong="H5631"\w* \w in charge of|strong="H8104"\w* \w the women|strong="H802"\w*, \w and let them be given|strong="H5414"\w* \w beauty treatments|strong="H8562"\w*. \v 4 \w Then let the young woman|strong="H5291"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w pleases|strong="H3190"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w become queen|strong="H4427"\w* \w in place|strong="H8478"\w* \w of Vashti|strong="H2060"\w*.”
\p \w This suggestion|strong="H1697"\w* \w pleased|strong="H3190"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w and he acted|strong="H6213"\w* \w accordingly|strong="H3651"\w*.
\s1 Esther Finds Favor
\p \v 5 \w Now there was|strong="H1961"\w* \w at the citadel|strong="H1002"\w* \w of Susa|strong="H7800"\w* \w a Jewish|strong="H3064"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w* \w from the tribe of Benjamin|strong="H1145"\w* \w named|strong="H8034"\w* \w Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Jair|strong="H2971"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Shimei|strong="H8096"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Kish|strong="H7027"\w*. \v 6 \w He|strong="H834"\w* \w had been carried into exile|strong="H1540"\w* \w from Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w by Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w among|strong="H5973"\w* \w those taken captive|strong="H1473"\w* \w with|strong="H5973"\w* \w Jeconiah|strong="H3204"\w*\f + \fr 2:6 \fqa Jeconiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 24:12|2KI 24:12\ref*.\f* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*.
\p \v 7 \w And Mordecai|strong="H1961"\w* \w had brought up|strong="H539"\w* \w Hadassah|strong="H1919"\w* \w (that is|strong="H1931"\w*, \w Esther|strong="H635"\w*), \w the daughter|strong="H1323"\w* \w of his uncle|strong="H1730"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w she did not|strong="H369"\w* have \w a father|strong="H1"\w* \w or mother|strong="H517"\w*. \w The young woman|strong="H5291"\w* \w was lovely|strong="H3303"\w* \w in form|strong="H8389"\w* \w and|strong="H2896"\w* \w appearance|strong="H4758"\w*, \w and when her father|strong="H1"\w* \w and mother|strong="H517"\w* \w had died|strong="H4194"\w*, \w Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w had taken her|strong="H3947"\w* as his own \w daughter|strong="H1323"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w When|strong="H1961"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w command|strong="H1697"\w* \w and edict|strong="H1881"\w* \w had been proclaimed|strong="H8085"\w*, \w many|strong="H7227"\w* \w young women|strong="H5291"\w* \w gathered|strong="H6908"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the citadel|strong="H1002"\w* \w of Susa|strong="H7800"\w* \w under|strong="H413"\w* \w the care|strong="H3027"\w* \w of Hegai|strong="H1896"\w*. \w Esther|strong="H635"\w* \w was also taken|strong="H3947"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the palace|strong="H1004"\w* \w and placed under|strong="H413"\w* \w the care|strong="H3027"\w* \w of Hegai|strong="H1896"\w*, \w the custodian|strong="H8104"\w* \w of the women|strong="H802"\w*. \v 9 \w And the young woman|strong="H5291"\w* \w pleased him|strong="H3190"\w* \w and obtained|strong="H5375"\w* \w his|strong="H6440"\w* \w favor|strong="H2617"\w*, \w so he quickly|strong="H926"\w* \w provided|strong="H5414"\w* her \w with beauty treatments|strong="H8562"\w* \w and the special diet|strong="H4490"\w*. \w He assigned|strong="H5414"\w* to her \w seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w select|strong="H7200"\w* \w maidservants|strong="H5291"\w* \w from the palace|strong="H1004"\w* \w and transferred her|strong="H8138"\w* \w with them|strong="H5291"\w* \w to the best|strong="H2896"\w* \w place|strong="H1004"\w* \w in the harem|strong="H802"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w Esther|strong="H635"\w* \w did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w reveal|strong="H5046"\w* \w her people|strong="H5971"\w* \w or|strong="H853"\w* \w her lineage|strong="H4138"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w had instructed|strong="H6680"\w* \w her|strong="H5921"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* \w to do so|strong="H5046"\w*. \v 11 \w And every day|strong="H3605"\w* \w Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w would walk back and forth|strong="H1980"\w* \w in front|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the court|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the harem|strong="H1004"\w* \w to learn|strong="H3045"\w* \w about|strong="H853"\w* \w Esther’s|strong="H635"\w* \w welfare|strong="H7965"\w* \w and what|strong="H4100"\w* \w was happening|strong="H6213"\w* to her.
\p \v 12 \w In the twelve|strong="H8147"\w* \w months|strong="H2320"\w* \w before her|strong="H5291"\w* \w turn|strong="H8447"\w* \w to go|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H325"\w*, \w the harem|strong="H802"\w* \w regulation required|strong="H1881"\w* \w each young woman|strong="H802"\w* \w to receive beauty treatments|strong="H4795"\w* \w with oil|strong="H8081"\w* \w of myrrh|strong="H4753"\w* \w for six|strong="H8337"\w* \w months|strong="H2320"\w*, \w and then with perfumes|strong="H1314"\w* \w and cosmetics|strong="H8562"\w* \w for another six|strong="H8337"\w* \w months|strong="H2320"\w*. \v 13 \w When|strong="H2088"\w* \w the young woman|strong="H5291"\w* \w would go|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w she was given|strong="H5414"\w* \w whatever|strong="H3605"\w* \w she requested|strong="H559"\w* \w to take|strong="H935"\w* \w with her|strong="H5973"\w* \w from the harem|strong="H1004"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w palace|strong="H1004"\w*. \v 14 \w She|strong="H1931"\w* \w would go there|strong="H935"\w* \w in the evening|strong="H6153"\w*, \w and in the morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w she|strong="H1931"\w* \w would return|strong="H7725"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w a second|strong="H8145"\w* \w harem|strong="H1004"\w*\f + \fr 2:14 \ft Or \fqa to another part of the harem\f* \w under|strong="H413"\w* \w the care|strong="H3027"\w* \w of Shaashgaz|strong="H8190"\w*, \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w eunuch|strong="H5631"\w* \w in charge of|strong="H8104"\w* \w the concubines|strong="H6370"\w*. \w She would not|strong="H3808"\w* \w return|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w unless|strong="H3588"\w* \w he|strong="H4428"\w* \w delighted|strong="H2654"\w* in her \w and summoned her|strong="H7121"\w* \w by name|strong="H8034"\w*.
\p \v 15 \w Now Esther|strong="H635"\w* \w was the daughter|strong="H1323"\w* \w of Abihail|strong="H32"\w*, \w the uncle|strong="H1730"\w* \w from whom Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w had adopted|strong="H3947"\w* her \w as his own daughter|strong="H1323"\w*. \w And when it was her turn|strong="H8447"\w* \w to go|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w she did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w ask for|strong="H1245"\w* \w anything|strong="H1697"\w* \w except|strong="H3588"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w Hegai|strong="H1896"\w*, \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w trusted official|strong="H5631"\w* \w in charge of|strong="H8104"\w* \w the harem|strong="H802"\w*, \w had advised|strong="H559"\w*. \w And Esther|strong="H635"\w* \w found|strong="H5375"\w* \w favor|strong="H2580"\w* \w in the eyes|strong="H5869"\w* \w of everyone|strong="H3605"\w* \w who saw her|strong="H7200"\w*.
