\p \v 5 \w Then Esther|strong="H635"\w* \w summoned|strong="H7121"\w* \w Hathach|strong="H2047"\w*, \w one of the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w eunuchs|strong="H5631"\w* \w appointed|strong="H5975"\w* \w to her|strong="H6440"\w*, \w and she dispatched him|strong="H6680"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w to learn|strong="H3045"\w* \w what was troubling him|strong="H4100"\w* \w and why|strong="H5921"\w*. \v 6 \w So Hathach|strong="H2047"\w* \w went out|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w square|strong="H7339"\w* \w in front|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w gate|strong="H8179"\w*, \v 7 \w and Mordecai|strong="H4782"\w* \w told|strong="H5046"\w* him \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w had happened to him|strong="H7136"\w*, \w including|strong="H853"\w* \w the exact amount|strong="H6575"\w* \w of money|strong="H3701"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Haman|strong="H2001"\w* \w had promised|strong="H559"\w* \w to pay|strong="H8254"\w* \w into|strong="H5921"\w* \w the royal|strong="H4428"\w* \w treasury|strong="H1595"\w* \w in order to destroy|strong="H6"\w* \w the Jews|strong="H3064"\w*.
